# Confidential client and reference material. Named customer folders are excluded
# locally via .git/info/exclude rather than here, so this file does not publish a
# customer list. If you keep client source material in this working tree, add it
# there, not to this file.

# The COR program library. The app is open source; this content is not. It is the
# deliverable of a paid build (policies, procedures, and forms written and mapped to
# a certifying partner's audit), and it is the part a template cannot replace.
# Untracked when the repo went open source.
/cor documents/

# Local QA exploration harness. state.json holds LIVE Supabase auth tokens, and the
# screenshots/logs are throwaway. Never commit these.
/playwright-explore/
/.cor_devserver.log

# Claude Code local settings hold a per-machine permission allowlist that can embed
# secrets (e.g. webhook bearer tokens) and local paths. Keep it out of git.
# .claude/launch.json (shared dev-server config) is tracked.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Working screenshots of a live admin console. These contain REAL personal data:
# worker names, job titles, and personal mobile numbers of people who never agreed
# to have it published. They were tracked by accident and are not product assets.
# Never commit a screenshot taken against real data; use the local seed fixtures
# (supabase/seed.sql) instead.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# Business strategy and commercial roadmap. These are working notes, not part of the
# product, and they carry pricing rationale and unreleased plans. They stay on disk in
# docs/ where they are convenient to work on, but git does not carry them. Technical docs
# that explain how the app works (the ELD map, the module specs) stay tracked on purpose:
# they help anyone self-hosting.
/docs/open-source-pivot-plan.md
/docs/ai-assistant-plan.md
/docs/inventory-tracking-plan.md
/docs/sales-deck/

# Internal working notes kept outside the repo. Not product documentation.
/SCREENSHOTS-INDEX.md
/agent.md.txt
